<!-- The D. Neb. supporting brief's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the
     face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 12 pt (size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 27.6
     pt line boxes (typst pitch-double, Word's double, as the exemplars are spaced) with a half-inch indent;
     the level 1 and certificate headings in them; the caption, level 2 and 3 headings, block quotations,
     signature and certificate lines in 13.8 pt boxes (typst pitch-single); letter page with 1-inch margins
     (NECivR 10.1(b)(1): 8 1/2 by 11 inch paper). The footer (typst footer-block): none on page 1 (w:titlePg,
     an empty first-page footer); from page 2 the page number centered, then 3 pt lower the paper's title at the
     left and "Case No." with the number at the right, 10 pt in exact 11.5 pt lines (typst pitch-footer); the
     footer distance (w:footer, 488 twips) is the one at which LibreOffice sets those lines on typst's baselines
     (footer-descent 30 %). The title and the number are the SUBJECT and COMMENTS document properties, which
     docx/ned-motion-brief.lua sets from the sample's frontmatter (footer_title, case_number), so no case text
     lives here. docx/ned-motion-brief.lua writes every body paragraph's own spacing. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
